# HTML email templates. Prettier rewrites the CSS inside <style> — it flips
# "Inconsolata" to 'Inconsolata', because the *.css singleQuote override only
# matches real .css files and embedded styles inherit singleQuote: true.
# Single-quoted font names are spec-valid but unreliable in Outlook's Word
# renderer, and email HTML depends on table layout and whitespace that a
# general-purpose formatter has no reason to respect. No upside here.
